description:
pkix-lint/src/lib.rs:1463-1469 — The Send+Sync compile-time assertion block added in commit c64dc840 only asserts Finding:

  const _: fn() = || {
      fn _assert_send_sync<T: Send + Sync>() {}
      _assert_send_sync::<Finding>();
  };

The commit message described "AGENTS.md non-negotiable #6 requires load-bearing result and error types to be Send+Sync." Finding satisfies this. The following public types ALSO load-bear under non-negotiable #6 and are not asserted:

LIB.RS:
- LintRunner (lib.rs:1142)
- LintResult (lib.rs:557)
- LintParameter (lib.rs:387)
- ParameterError (lib.rs:498)

DEVIATION.RS:
- Deviation (deviation.rs:127)
- DeviationScope (deviation.rs:467)
- DeviationStore (deviation.rs:855)
- DeviationAddError (deviation.rs:69)
- DeviationRunResult (deviation.rs:1062)
- DeviationRunner (deviation.rs:1112)
- ScopePropValue (deviation.rs:445)
- DeviatedFinding (report.rs:13)

REPORT.RS:
- EvaluationReport (report.rs:61)

OSCAL:
- ParseError (oscal/parse.rs:43) — separately flagged for missing Clone derives, but Send+Sync untested here too
- ResolvedProfile (oscal/profile.rs:102)

Every type listed satisfies Send+Sync today (auto-derived from its fields). The point of the assertion block is to PIN that invariant against future regression: a maintainer who adds an Rc<T>, RefCell<T>, or unsync interior cache field will not catch the breakage at compile time without an assertion.

CALLER IMPACT: A caller depending on these types being Send+Sync for cross-thread caching, async tasks, or rayon-style batch evaluation gets silent breakage on the version that adds the offending field. The "cache-friendly result types" requirement in non-negotiable #6 cannot be relied on for any type other than Finding.

REMEDIATION: Extend the const _: fn() block at lib.rs:1463 to assert every public result, error, config, and value-carrier type. ~15 additional _assert_send_sync calls. Pre-1.0 free.

Suggested grouping:
  // Lint-engine surface
  _assert_send_sync::<LintRunner>();
  _assert_send_sync::<LintResult>();
  _assert_send_sync::<LintParameter>();
  _assert_send_sync::<ParameterError>();
  // Deviation surface
  _assert_send_sync::<Deviation>();
  _assert_send_sync::<DeviationScope>();
  _assert_send_sync::<DeviationStore>();
  _assert_send_sync::<DeviationAddError>();
  _assert_send_sync::<DeviationRunResult>();
  _assert_send_sync::<DeviationRunner>();
  _assert_send_sync::<ScopePropValue>();
  _assert_send_sync::<DeviatedFinding>();
  // Report surface
  _assert_send_sync::<EvaluationReport>();
  // OSCAL surface (oscal feature only — gate with #[cfg])
  #[cfg(feature = "oscal")]
  _assert_send_sync::<crate::oscal::parse::ParseError>();
  #[cfg(feature = "oscal")]
  _assert_send_sync::<crate::oscal::profile::ResolvedProfile>();
